{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared Excel-semantics case table for the PlexiSum formula engines.",
    "Committed to plexichat as src/tests/suite/formula_parity_cases.json and to",
    "plexichat-client as tests/unit/data/formula-parity-cases.json. The two",
    "copies must stay byte-identical: each engine is tested against the copy it",
    "ships, and every expected value is what Excel returns, so either engine",
    "drifting from Excel (or from the other engine) fails a test.",
    "Types are explicit (number:/text:/boolean:/error:/blank) so a text \"12\" is",
    "never mistaken for the number 12.",
    "Cells A1:F6 hold the fixture data below; an unlisted cell is blank."
  ],
  "sheet": "1",
  "grid": {
    "A1": 1,
    "A2": 2,
    "A3": 3,
    "A4": "x",
    "A5": {
      "formula": "1/0"
    },
    "A6": "7",
    "B1": "one",
    "B2": "two",
    "B3": "three",
    "B4": "",
    "B6": true,
    "C1": 10,
    "C2": 20,
    "C3": 30,
    "D1": "apple",
    "D2": "banana",
    "D3": "cherry",
    "F1": "2abc",
    "F2": "5",
    "F3": true
  },
